  "rendered": "The table lists three lipid-based carriers, two under passive targeting and one under active targeting.[1][2]Table 2[3] Under passive targeting, the Cationic lipids[4] system shelled with mPEG-DMG[5] (delivering MBD2 siRNA[6]) has a particle size of ~98 nm[7] and releases cargo via the Proton Sponge Effect[8]. The LNPs[9] carrying si-FOXM1[10] are reported at 90–100 nm[11] with release by Intracellular/Lysosomal Escape[12]. Under active targeting, the LNP[13] decorated with M2pep[14] and delivering siITGB4[15] is ~150 nm[16] in size with a PH-Responsive Release[17] mechanism. So the lipid carriers span a narrow size range of roughly one hundred to one hundred fifty nanometres, while their release mechanisms differ: endosomal buffering for the cationic lipid formulation, lysosomal escape for the plain LNPs, and acidic-pH triggering for the peptide-decorated LNP.",
